  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129776",
      "title": "Building Custom Validators",
      "lectureOrder": 255,
      "videoOrder": 243,
      "sourceHash": "ec11584e48ee62f4e1a92a1effb18ec02fe2e6edf2f55d60433a24397603c139",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 3.51,
          "en": "So we added validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.51,
          "end": 4.83,
          "en": "I did mention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.83,
          "end": 8.94,
          "en": "that we would also build our own custom validator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 11.357,
          "en": "and that is indeed what I'll do now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.357,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "because thankfully that's really straightforward,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 19.17,
          "en": "especially when working with reactive forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.17,
          "end": 22.32,
          "en": "When it comes to template driven forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.32,
          "end": 25.53,
          "en": "adding your own validator is a bit more complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.53,
          "end": 30.24,
          "en": "because you need to build your own validation directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.24,
          "end": 32.616,
          "en": "and register it with Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.616,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "and also implement certain features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 39.603,
          "en": "Angular expects from validation directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.04,
          "end": 46.02,
          "en": "That's why you might not end up building custom validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 48.87,
          "en": "for template driven forms too often,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 51.03,
          "en": "especially since Angular ships",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 52.98,
          "en": "with many built in validators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.98,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "which cover all common use cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "But if you ever need to build your own validator directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "or if you want to do that, attached you find a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 66.36,
          "en": "to the official Angular documentation where you can learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "how to create such a validation directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "It's not super complex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "just a bit more complex than building validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 78.24,
          "en": "for reactive forms, as you will see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.24,
          "end": 81.48,
          "en": "Because a validator for a reactive form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 85.38,
          "en": "let's say for this password form input here is in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.38,
          "end": 86.776,
          "en": "just a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.776,
          "end": 91.05,
          "en": "A function which will automatically get that control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.05,
          "end": 93.976,
          "en": "as an input and a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.976,
          "end": 96.39,
          "en": "that should then return null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.39,
          "end": 100.712,
          "en": "or nothing if the control is considered to be valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.712,
          "end": 104.7,
          "en": "from this validator's point of view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "Or return anything else, for example, an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 111.87299999999999,
          "en": "with details about the error if it's considered invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 116.25,
          "en": "Now here, I'll actually outsource this into a separate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.25,
          "end": 118.5,
          "en": "standalone function which I'll store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.5,
          "end": 120.9,
          "en": "in this same file though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.9,
          "end": 123,
          "en": "You could also put it into a separate file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123,
          "end": 126.36,
          "en": "but to keep things together, I'll keep it in this file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 131.36,
          "en": "and I'll name this function must contain question mark,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.78,
          "end": 136.14,
          "en": "because here I want to build a simple dummy validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.14,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "function that ensures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 141.123,
          "en": "that my password contains at least one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.123,
          "end": 143.313,
          "en": "question mark character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.15,
          "end": 147.39,
          "en": "So as mentioned, we'll get a control as an input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 151.56,
          "en": "and that will be a so-called abstract control,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 155.779,
          "en": "which is a type that must be imported from Angular forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.779,
          "end": 159.03300000000002,
          "en": "So that's the kind of value we get as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.07999999999998,
          "end": 165.07999999999998,
          "en": "And then here I want to check if control.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 167.733,
          "en": "contains a question mark,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.6,
          "end": 172.413,
          "en": "and we can do this pretty easily with this JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.25,
          "end": 176.16,
          "en": "If that's the case, I'll return null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.16,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "and that will tell Angular that this control is valid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 184.95,
          "en": "at least from this validator's point of view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 187.87,
          "en": "But alternatively, I'll return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.63,
          "end": 193.86,
          "en": "where I'll have a property which I'll name does not contain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 193.86,
          "end": 197.073,
          "en": "question mark, which I'll set to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 197.97,
          "end": 200.55,
          "en": "You can structure this object however you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 200.55,
          "end": 203.79,
          "en": "That's just a common convention that you have some kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.79,
          "end": 207.84,
          "en": "of descriptive error code, which is set to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.84,
          "end": 211.44,
          "en": "So now with that, this function is finished though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "that should be includes, not contains.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 218.19,
          "en": "Includes is the right one. I always mess these two up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.19,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "But includes is a built-in method built into JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "which can be called on strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 226.077,
          "en": "to check whether a string includes a certain character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 226.077,
          "end": 229.59,
          "en": "And with that, this validation function is now finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 229.59,
          "end": 232.263,
          "en": "and we can now go down to our password control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.263,
          "end": 235.59300000000002,
          "en": "and add it here to this validator's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 236.49,
          "end": 239.389,
          "en": "I'm not executing it here, instead I'm just passing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.389,
          "end": 243.3,
          "en": "as a pointer to this function, to this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.3,
          "end": 246.27,
          "en": "because Angular will execute these validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 246.27,
          "end": 247.563,
          "en": "functions for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 248.4,
          "end": 250.35,
          "en": "Min length was executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250.35,
          "end": 253.05,
          "en": "because that's actually a factory function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 256.38,
          "en": "that produces the validator function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.38,
          "end": 259.337,
          "en": "That's a pattern you can use if you have a validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.337,
          "end": 262.05,
          "en": "function that needs some configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.05,
          "end": 265.35,
          "en": "like the minimum length for which it should check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 265.35,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "But that's not the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 269.073,
          "en": "for our custom validator function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.24,
          "end": 273.353,
          "en": "And with that all, if we now go back to our form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.353,
          "end": 276.36,
          "en": "I can enter a valid email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 279.09000000000003,
          "en": "But if I now enter a super long password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.09000000000003,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "which does not include a question mark, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 283.383,
          "en": "I get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 287.76,
          "en": "And we probably should clarify the error message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287.76,
          "end": 290.82,
          "en": "to make it clear that we need a question mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 290.82,
          "end": 295.263,
          "en": "because as soon as I add one here, this error goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297,
          "end": 298.71,
          "en": "And that's there how we can build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.71,
          "end": 301.233,
          "en": "and register our own validator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 302.31,
          "end": 305.34,
          "en": "Now, I'll just quickly go to the login component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.34,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "and update this error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 310.59,
          "en": "and say, must be at least six characters long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 310.59,
          "end": 313.533,
          "en": "and contain a question mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.67,
          "end": 315.503,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 317.25,
          "end": 320.763,
          "en": "But with that, this is now finished.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
